# Firebase TTS shared-cache config (example — copy to `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev`,
# or `wrangler secret put` each value for production. NEVER commit the real `.dev.vars`.)
#
# 1. Create a Firebase project (free Spark plan): https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Add a Web App — copy its web API key + Project ID below.
# 3. Firestore: create a database (us-central1 or nearest), start in test mode, then
#    paste the Security Rules from README ("Firebase TTS cache setup").
# 4. (Optional) Add a 7-day TTL on the `createdAt` field for a free native prune.
#
# These are read by src/lib/pollyCache.ts. If unset, caching is disabled and the app
# falls straight through to live AWS Polly.

FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-web-api-key
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id

# AWS Polly (required for actual synthesis; cache only stores the results)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA...
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Optional: lower the free-tier cap (default 50000 docs ≈ 500 MB)
# POLLY_CACHE_MAX_DOCS=50000
